<p>Israel said it will begin direct talks with Lebanon, with U.S.-hosted meetings expected in Washington next week, even as Israeli strikes on Lebanon continued and Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu said there is &quot;no ceasefire in Lebanon&quot;. The new diplomatic track opens as Washington tries to keep the fragile U.S.-Iran ceasefire from unraveling. Lebanon is now the most immediate test of whether the wider truce can hold.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/ABpMdeXZVVkGcpc7V1U6N9Fb7Arb9ETqIU9L0KK4D7-T7o0qEmzxQhPHYn9BdBsuHtPnn8kc6XQE469ZRm0aGYyJNsPHYh9aBL0t_SJ8EEq9' alt='Heavy machinery operates at the site of an Israeli strike carried out on Wednesday, in Ain Al Mraiseh in Beirut, Lebanon on April 9, 2026.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Ceasefire-first sequencing: Lebanese officials said Beirut spent the previous 24 hours pushing for a temporary ceasefire before formal negotiations, underscoring how far apart the two sides still are on the order of steps.</li><li>Civilian expectation gap: Many in Lebanon assumed the U.S.-brokered ceasefire would protect the country too, showing how disputed the truce&#x27;s geographic scope has become.</li><li>Bigger stated goal: Netanyahu&#x27;s office described the proposed channel as a way not only to discuss Hezbollah but also to seek &quot;peace&quot; or formal relations between the two neighbors.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Israeli government: Netanyahu said he instructed ministers to begin direct negotiations with Lebanon centered on disarming Hezbollah, while insisting Israel would keep striking Hezbollah because no ceasefire exists in Lebanon. (<a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/04/09/world/middleeast/israel-lebanon-talks-hezbollah-disarm.html'>The New York Times</a>)</li><li>Lebanese government: A Lebanese official said Beirut wants a ceasefire in place before talks begin, reflecting concern that negotiations cannot move forward credibly while bombardment continues. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1990283/israel-seeks-peace-talks-with-lebanon-as-soon-as-possible-as-world-condemns-tel-avivs-bombardment-amid-us-iran-truce'>Dawn</a>)</li><li>Iran: Iranian leaders said Lebanon should be included in the ceasefire and warned that continued Israeli attacks could make planned dialogue with Washington meaningless. (<a href='https://english.elpais.com/international/2026-04-09/netanyahu-digs-in-on-his-war-in-lebanon-as-iran-warns-that-dialogue-with-the-united-states-will-become-meaningless.html'>El País</a>)</li><li>United States: U.S. officials pushed Israel to accept direct talks with Lebanon as Washington tried to shore up the shaky truce with Iran and keep the diplomatic channel open. (<a href='https://www.axios.com/2026/04/09/israel-lebanon-negotiations-ceasefire'>Axios</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.semafor.com/article/04/09/2026/israel-lebanon-to-hold-direct-talks'>Israel, Lebanon to hold direct talks</a> - semafor.com</li><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/live/2026/04/09/world/iran-ceasefire-trump-lebanon'>Israel Agrees to Talks With Lebanon but Keeps Striking Hezbollah</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.ndtv.com/world-news/iran-us-ceasefire-will-bomb-tel-aviv-if-firing-doesnt-stop-in-lebanon-iran-warns-israel-11327765#publisher=newsstand'>Iran-US Ceasefire: &quot;Will Bomb Tel Aviv If Firing Doesn&#x27;t Stop In Lebanon&quot;: Iran Warns Israel</a> - ndtv.com</li><li><a href='https://english.elpais.com/international/2026-04-09/netanyahu-digs-in-on-his-war-in-lebanon-as-iran-warns-that-dialogue-with-the-united-states-will-become-meaningless.html'>Netanyahu digs in on his war in Lebanon, as Iran warns that dialogue with the United States will become ‘meaningless’</a> - elpais.com</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/netanyahu-authorises-direct-talks-with-lebanon-as-soon-as-possible/article70844250.ece'>Netanyahu authorises direct talks with Lebanon &#x27;as soon as possible&#x27;</a> - 